course: dictionary
lesson: 729
title: Words for games and sport
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have two meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Baseball» can be the name of a game or the name of the ball used in it. Read the words around it to decide.
explain: «In baseball a run means getting round all four bases.» Here baseball is the game, because the sentence is about runs and bases. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then try your meaning in place of the word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Words can also work as a describing word. «Baseball cap», «baseball card» and «baseball team» use baseball to tell you what kind of cap, card or team it is. When you see a word in front of another word, it may be describing it.
fact: Baseball is a game where two teams of 9 take turns to hit a ball with a bat and run round four bases.
fact: A baseball is the hard, white ball used in this game.
fact: In baseball, three strikes and the batter is out, and four balls means the batter walks to first base.
fact: Baseball is a popular sport in the USA and Canada.
fact: Context clues help you work out which meaning of a word is being used.
exercise: «In baseball a run means getting round all four bases.» How many bases must a runner get round? | Two | Three | Six | *Four
exercise: «In baseball and softball the batter wears a helmet and drops the bat after hitting.» What must the batter wear? | Shin pads | *A helmet | Nothing at all | A cap
exercise: In Ohio, Lorcan goes to a family reunion and plays baseball with his cousins all day. What is Lorcan doing with them? | Sleeping in the sun | Eating a picnic | *Playing a game | Reading a book
test: In baseball, how many players are on each team? | Six | Twelve | *Nine | Eleven
test: «In baseball three strikes and the batter is out.» What happens after three strikes? | *The batter is out | The batter walks to first base | The game stops for lunch | A run scores
exam: Which one is a baseball? | A bat for hitting the ball | *A hard, white ball used in the game | A soft red ball for the park | A cap worn on the head
